## 🧠 Key Takeaways

* Linux permissions control access to files and directories.
* `chmod` changes permissions.
* `chown` changes ownership.
* ACL provides granular access control.
* SUID affects executable effective UID.
* SGID affects executable effective GID and directory group inheritance.
* Sticky Bit protects entries in shared directories.
* Least privilege is preferable to unrestricted permissions.

